Rights notice for the contents of data/

The MIT License in the repository root covers the OnceOnly source code only.
It does NOT apply to this directory.

What is licensed, and by whom
- The Berkeley Carbon Trading Project releases the Voluntary Registry Offsets
  Database v2026-08 under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
  (CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ . That is the
  licence Berkeley states on its download page and in the workbook. We use and
  attribute the data on that basis.

What we could not verify
- The rows in data/reference/ originate from the Verra and Gold Standard
  registries. The Berkeley "registry files" workbook we parse describes them as
  "exactly as downloaded" from the registries and carries no licence statement
  of its own.
- Verra's Registry Terms of Use (July 2026) and the Gold Standard Impact
  Registry Terms of Use (v2.1, May 2025) state that the registry owns its data
  and restrict copying or sharing of registry contents with third parties
  without written permission. Neither document, as far as we could find, grants
  a licence to third parties to redistribute registry records, and we could not
  confirm that Berkeley holds registry permission to relicense these rows.
- We therefore make no claim that the registry-origin rows in this directory
  are freely redistributable. They are included only so that the
  demonstration and tests run without a 67 MB download, and for the
  non-commercial hackathon evaluation of this project. If you are a rights
  holder and want any of this removed, open an issue or contact the repository
  owner and it will be removed promptly.
- This notice is not legal advice.

What is in this directory
- data/reference/: a 38,004-row subset of registry records (Verra retirements
  and issuances, Gold Standard retirements), reformatted into registry, batch
  and unit ranges. It includes the beneficiary and reason text where the
  registries publish it.
- data/demo/: fictional claim documents that quote real registry serial ranges.
  The claimants and statements are invented and labelled SYNTHETIC.
- data/raw/ (not committed): the downloaded source workbooks. Rebuild the full
  index yourself with `make data`, which downloads from Berkeley.

Required attribution (kept everywhere the data is used)
  Quartson, P., Haya, B.K., Bernard, T., Abayo, A., Rong, X., So, I.S., Elias, M. (2026).
  Voluntary Registry Offsets Database v2026-08, Berkeley Carbon Trading Project,
  UC Berkeley. https://gspp.berkeley.edu/berkeley-carbon-trading-project/offsets-database
  Registry data (c) the respective registries (Verra, Gold Standard).

Changes made by OnceOnly: rows were selected to cover the demo scenarios and
reformatted (parsed into registry, batch and unit ranges). No endorsement by
the Berkeley Carbon Trading Project or the registries is implied.
